  "grammar": {
    "title": "Articles: A, An and The",
    "explanation": "Use **a** or **an** when you talk about one thing for the first time. It is not a special thing.\n\nUse **an** before a vowel sound. It is the sound, not the letter.\n\nUse **the** when the listener knows which thing you mean. You both know it.\n\nUse **the** when we talk about the same thing again. First **a**, then **the**.\n\nUse **the** when there is only one. **The** sun. **The** moon.\n\nUse no article with plural nouns and uncountable nouns in general.\n\nJobs need **a** or **an**. She is **a** doctor.",
    "examples": [
      "*I have **a** brother and **a** sister.* (first mention)",
      "*She's **an** English teacher.* (a job; vowel sound)",
      "*Can you open **the** window, please?* (we know which window)",
      "*We bought **a** car. **The** car is red.* (first mention, then second mention)",
      "*It takes **an** hour to get there.* (the h is silent)",
      "*He goes to **work** by bus.* (no article)"
    ],
    "practice": [
      {
        "q": "Rewrite with **a**: She is ___ doctor.",
        "a": "She is a doctor."
      },
      {
        "q": "Rewrite with **an**: I eat ___ apple every day.",
        "a": "I eat an apple every day."
      },
      {
        "q": "Rewrite with **the**: I see a ring. ___ ring is gold.",
        "a": "The ring is gold."
      },
      {
        "q": "Fix the mistake: I need an advice.",
        "a": "I need some advice."
      }
    ],
